WEBVTT

NOTE On-screen visual text only; this approved video has no audio track.

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.667
A visual document contains a sentence attempting to order an unrelated action.

2
00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:14.517
The system records its origin as received content, not application policy.

3
00:00:14.517 --> 00:00:21.867
Correctly reading an instruction does not give it authority to change permissions.

4
00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:29.217
The model proposes sending a record to an external destination.

5
00:00:29.217 --> 00:00:36.067
The controller checks permission and denies egress before execution.

6
00:00:36.067 --> 00:00:43.417
Logging the attempt after sending would not have prevented disclosure.

7
00:00:43.917 --> 00:00:50.767
An image contains a visible name and separate location metadata.

8
00:00:50.767 --> 00:00:57.617
Covering the name pixels does not automatically alter the metadata.

9
00:00:57.617 --> 00:01:04.967
Each channel needs review; this example contains no real personal data.

10
00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:12.317
An altered document copy states an amount different from the original.

11
00:01:12.317 --> 00:01:19.167
Once indexed, future queries can repeatedly retrieve that copy.

12
00:01:19.167 --> 00:01:27.583
Versioning, validation and removal affect retrieval; they are not equivalent to retraining model weights.

13
00:01:28.083 --> 00:01:34.933
Perception produces a proposal to modify record A.

14
00:01:34.933 --> 00:01:42.100
Before committing, the object, change and scope are shown to the authorized reviewer.

15
00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:50.517
Without authorization the change is not applied; valid approval still does not guarantee perception was correct.

16
00:01:51.017 --> 00:01:57.867
In this example, nineteen of twenty bright images are answered correctly.

17
00:01:57.867 --> 00:02:05.033
Under low light, only twelve of twenty succeed, even if the combined average looks better.

18
00:02:05.033 --> 00:02:12.700
Keep conditions and sample sizes; do not attribute these invented results to a real model.

